leaf-key.pkcs8.b64 is the PKCS#8 DER private key matching LEAF_CERTIFICATE_DER_BASE64
in tests/fixtures.ts, base64 encoded so WebCrypto can import it directly.

It is a throwaway key generated by openssl for tests. It signs nothing real, it is
not stored by the plugin, and it must never be treated as a credential.

signed-by-us.xml is a SAML Response signed by this plugin's own sign.ts using that
key. It is regenerated by `packages/frontend/src/core/saml/interop.spec.ts`, which
asserts our signer still produces these exact bytes.

The bytes were validated by an independent XML-DSig implementation before being
committed. See the verification record at the bottom of this file.

Independent verification record, 2026-08-06
-------------------------------------------
signed-by-us.xml was verified by signxml 5.1.0 (a pure-Python XML-DSig
implementation, unrelated to this codebase) against the leaf certificate:

  SIGNXML: VERIFIED   signed element: Assertion

Negative controls, all rejected as expected:
  subject changed alice -> admin        InvalidDigest    "Digest mismatch for reference 0 (#_a1)"
  one byte of SignatureValue flipped    InvalidSignature
  verified against a different cert     InvalidSignature

The same tool verifies the real Shibboleth capture in tests/captures, which
confirms it handles this document shape rather than accepting anything.

Regenerating signed-by-us.xml
-----------------------------
Only needed when signing deliberately changes. In interop.spec.ts, temporarily
write outcome.xml to signed-by-us.xml, run the spec once, remove the write, then
re-run the independent verification above and update this record. Never update
the golden without re-running that verification: the golden's only value is that
an implementation we did not write accepted these exact bytes.
